## Finding 1 (fixable): the "empty Gemfile.lock diff" check is wrong, and following it breaks CI

Plan Test Plan, step 1.3, Challenges, and Pre-Mortem, plus brief Requirement 4 and AC2, say `bundle _2.6.9_ install` must leave `Gemfile.lock` with an empty diff, and tell the builder to restore the lockfile if it changes. I ran this in a temp copy with all 11 pins applied. Every locked version satisfies its `~>` range, and no `GEM` or `specs` entry moves. But the lockfile `DEPENDENCIES` section does change: bundler records each constraint, so 11 lines go from `bigdecimal` to `bigdecimal (~> 4.1)`, and so on. The diff is not empty. It is a 16-line change (`diff` hunks at 188-189, 192, 194, 197, 199-204).

This matters because `.github/workflows/pr-check.yaml` uses `ruby/setup-ruby` with `bundler-cache: true`, which turns on frozen/deployment mode. I reproduced that with `BUNDLE_FROZEN=true`: with the new Gemfile and the old lockfile, `bundle install` exits 16 ("Some dependencies were deleted from your gemfile, but the lockfile can't be updated because frozen mode is set"). So the plan's "restore the lockfile" fallback would produce a PR that fails CI. The updated `Gemfile.lock` has to be committed with the Gemfile.

Required plan change: replace "empty `Gemfile.lock` diff" with "the only `Gemfile.lock` change is the `DEPENDENCIES` section gaining the 11 `~>` constraints, and no `specs`, `PLATFORMS`, or `BUNDLED WITH` lines change." Commit the lockfile with the Gemfile. Check with `BUNDLE_FROZEN=true bundle _2.6.9_ install --local`. Reword Requirement 4 and AC2 to "no resolution change" (AC2 already says that; Requirement 4 says "unchanged"). Update the Challenges and Pre-Mortem bullets to match. I did not edit the plan; the judge-do-not-fix rule applies.

