## Advisories

A1. Label: the plan marks Gemfile, Dockerfile, and dependabot.yml as "prose/policy". always-tdd lists configuration the product runs as executable. The no-test outcome is still right, because the only tests available are change-detectors, and the contract between Gemfile and lockfile is already enforced by pr-check. Say that in the plan instead of the prose label.

A2. Radical innovation (advisory only): add a `bundle check`-style lockstep gate to the unit tests or pr-check, such as `BUNDLE_FROZEN=true bundle install --local` run before the Jekyll build. A Gemfile and lockfile that drift apart would then fail fast with a clear message. pr-check already fails in this case, but only inside the setup-ruby cache step. A named step would cost about 3 lines of YAML. It is out of scope for this task.

A3. The proposed Dependabot `docker` entry on `/nginx-proxy` will propose bumps across the `nginx` tag line, not only `-alpine3.22`. Constraint 1 in the brief expects `-alpine3.22` suffix bumps. Dependabot generally keeps the suffix, but check the first PR it opens. Add `ignore` entries if it proposes a different Alpine base.
